        {
          "kicker": "Player move",
          "heading": "Billy Searle turns down France return to stay at Leicester Tigers",
          "body": "Leicester fly-half Billy Searle turned down a potential return to France to stay at Welford Road, telling BBC Radio Leicester he wanted to \"push his game on\" in England. The 30-year-old signed a three-year extension in September, having already had three spells in French rugby, at Toulouse, Biarritz and Agen. \"I had interest in France but I made it clear I wanted to stay,\" he said. He also hasn't given up on a first senior England cap."
