          "heading": "Taulupe Faletau needs finger surgery, Wales hope he's back for November",
          "body": "Faletau's comeback has come undone. The Cardiff number eight, 35 and on 109 Wales caps, will have surgery on a finger injured in his first game since March, and he misses the URC derby at Ospreys. Cardiff head coach Corniel van Zyl said: \"He will miss the Ospreys game but hopefully after November he will be fine.\" Steve Tandy left him out of the Nations Championship squad and has said he needs to show durability before any return."
