      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tactical analysis",
          "heading": "Springboks' eight defeats since 2023 read like a manual for beating them",
          "body": "Planet Rugby's analysis argues South Africa's eight Test defeats since the start of 2023 read like a coaching manual for beating the world champions. The winning side averaged 29.9 points across the eight, and none of them scored fewer tries than the Springboks did, so scoring capacity is the first thing the evidence asks for. The Springboks face Italy, France and Ireland in the November leg of the Nations Championship."
        },
